"""MPSP JPS with lazily-filled jump-distance tables.

__init__ is cheap: tables start as [-1]*n_pad (sentinel "uncomputed").
During plan(), each time a table entry is read for the first time,
_fill_j<dir> walks the ray from that cell back-filling every cell along the
way up to the next JP / wall / already-cached cell. Cells filled by plan() #1
stay filled for plan() #2 — that's the Mpsp contract in practice.

Diagonal fills require the two perpendicular cardinals be filled at the
intermediate cell first; each _fill_j<NE|SE|SW|NW> does that inline.

Entry direction encoding: (dx+1)*3 + (dy+1) in [0, 8]; enc=4 unused.
"""

